# scenarios/7_customer_deposit.books: loaded by ledger_server into 7_customer_deposit.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	7. A customer's deposit: money in, but no revenue yet
about	A deposit paid before the goods are delivered is not revenue: the company owes the goods, or the money back. It sits in Customer deposits, a liability (acomptes reçus, ontvangen vooruitbetalingen), until the delivery.
about	On delivery the whole 10,000 is invoiced and becomes revenue, and the deposit is set against the invoice: the customer owes only the 7,000 left.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Capital
account	550000	asset	Bank account
account	400001	asset	Customer 1
account	460000	liability	Customer deposits
account	700000	revenue	Sales
entry	2011-01-02	The founder puts in savings
posting	Capital	-500000
posting	Bank account	500000
entry	2011-02-01	Customer 1 pays a 30% deposit on an order of 10,000
posting	Customer deposits	-300000
posting	Bank account	300000
entry	2011-03-15	The goods are delivered and invoiced: 10,000
posting	Sales	-1000000
posting	Customer 1	1000000
entry	2011-03-15	The deposit is set against the invoice
posting	Customer 1	-300000
posting	Customer deposits	300000
entry	2011-04-15	Customer 1 pays the 7,000 left
posting	Customer 1	-700000
posting	Bank account	700000
